  "cover_text": "When people ask me what my favorite horror film is, one answer hits me right to the chest: \"The Haunting Train.\"\nI watched it when I was in school in the early 1960s and never forgot. It left such a mark on my mind that I have continued to seek out similar foundation horror films throughout the years.\nIt is a movie about a man, played by Gary Sinise, who, after losing his wife, acquires a romance with a woman named Martha Penn by flipping a table over. Although it seems well-capitalized, Sinise's film wouldn't have been even remotely funny and at no point did the scene with a bullet ricochet off his car ve",
